---
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`Privacy | ${site.name}`}
  description="How SGLA handles the information you share through this website."
  heading="Privacy"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>Who this covers</h2>
  <p>
    This notice explains what happens to information you share with {site.name} through
    <a href={site.url}>sgla.co.uk</a>. The data controller is {site.name}, based in
    {site.location}, and you can get in touch through the
    <a href={site.cta.href}>contact form</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the contact form, the details you enter (your name, business, email address,
    website address and message) are recorded as an enquiry in Zoho CRM, which {site.name} uses to
    keep track of enquiries and reply to them. Zoho processes this information on my behalf and
    stores it on servers in the European Union. Submissions aren't stored in a database on this
    website itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    I keep these enquiries for as long as needed to answer them and, if we work together, for the
    duration of the project and a reasonable period afterwards for record-keeping. The legal basis
    for this is legitimate interest in responding to enquiries and, where relevant, taking steps to
    enter into a contract. I don't use your details for marketing, and I don't sell or pass them to
    anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Vercel Web Analytics to understand roughly how many people visit and which pages
    they look at. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't track you across other websites, and doesn't store
    personal data that identifies you. Because of this, there's no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel's servers process standard technical
    data such as IP addresses when delivering pages, in line with Vercel's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK GDPR you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information I hold about you.
    Send the request through the <a href={site.cta.href}>contact form</a> and I'll deal with it
    promptly, and within one month at the latest. If you're not happy with how I've handled your
    data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this notice changes, the updated version will be published here with a new date.</p>
</LegalLayout>
